# Rottenmouth Viper's rulings: each opponent makes all their choices, then the sacrifices, discards and losses of life all
# happen at the same time (CR 101.4). Bot2 Show and Tells Platinum Emperion ("Your life total can't change") in beside Bot1's
# Viper, and chooses to lose 4 life for its first counter: the Emperion stops that loss (CR 119.7). On turn 3 the Viper attacks with two counters and Bot2 chooses to sacrifice the Emperion for one and
# to lose 4 life for the other: the Emperion is still on the battlefield as that loss would happen, so its life total can't
# change and it loses none. Only then is it gone, and the Viper's 6 combat damage is lost: 20 - 6 = 14 (not 10, as it would
# be had the sacrifice come first).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Rottenmouth Viper
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Platinum Emperion
Lightning Bolt x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Rottenmouth Viper)
Bot2.Choose(Platinum Emperion)
Bot2.Modes(Lose 4 life)
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot2.Battlefield = Platinum Emperion
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Rottenmouth Viper > Bot2)
Bot2.Modes(Sacrifice a nonland permanent)
Bot2.Choose(Platinum Emperion)
Bot2.Modes(Lose 4 life)
? Bot2.Graveyard = Platinum Emperion
? Bot2.Life = 20
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 14
Bot1.Battlefield.Rottenmouth Viper.Counters.Blight = 2
Bot2.Graveyard = Platinum Emperion
